# Snugbox audit of web-1

This box pays for 8 GiB and needs 2.84 GiB. A 4 GiB plan fits.

Snugbox 1.0.0, Sat 31 Oct 2026 09:01 +00:00. Read-only: it changed nothing and sent no data.

## Summary

| | | |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Pays for | 8 GiB | DigitalOcean Basic 8 GiB, $48.00 a month |
| Needs | 2.84 GiB | snug size: 2.34 need + 0.25 headroom + 0.25 cache |
| Waste | 5.16 GiB | |
| Fits | 4 GiB | Basic 4 GiB, new server, saves $24.00 a month |
| Confidence | low | Early estimate from 60 seconds of data. Keep watching for a week before changing plans. |

## Risks

- No swap, and no early out-of-memory protection.
- 2 of 2 containers have no memory limit: shop-app-1, shop-db-1.
- No out-of-memory kills since the box booted 10 days ago, and pressure stayed under 1% since boot.

## Workloads

Working set is the memory a workload would miss if it were taken away: memory that can't be dropped plus the file cache it keeps rereading.

| Workload | Kind | Program | 95th pct | 99th pct | Peak seen | memory.peak | Limit |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| shop-app-1 | container | node | 1,280 MiB | 1,280 MiB | 1,280 MiB | 1,600 MiB | none |
| shop-db-1 | container | postgres | 628 MiB | 628 MiB | 628 MiB | 1,028 MiB | none |
| backup.service | service | restic | 300 MiB | 300 MiB | 300 MiB | 300 MiB | none |
| ssh.service | service | sshd | 6 MiB | 6 MiB | 6 MiB | 6 MiB | none |
| cron.service | service | cron | 0.3 MiB | 0.3 MiB | 0.3 MiB | 0.3 MiB | none |
| Kernel and other | kernel | | 178 MiB | 178 MiB | 178 MiB | | |

## Fixes

| # | Fix | Risk |
| ---: | --- | --- |
| 1 | Limits for shop-app-1 | medium |
| 2 | Limits for backup.service | medium |
| 3 | Early out-of-memory protection, systemd-oomd | medium |
| 4 | Heap caps for shop-app-1, after a restart | medium to high |

Preview a fix with `snugbox fit --dry-run <number>` and apply it with `sudo snugbox fit <number>`. Every fix has an undo: `sudo snugbox undo --last`.

- shop-app-1: limit 1,664 MiB, reservation 1,280 MiB, an early estimate.
- backup.service: MemoryMax 448 MiB, MemoryHigh 384 MiB, an early estimate.
- shop-app-1, Node.js: set `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=1248` in its environment when you next make the container.

Note: shop-db-1 is PostgreSQL and holds 628 MiB, 128 MiB of it shared memory, which is mostly shared\_buffers. On Vultr vc2-2c-4gb, shared\_buffers plus max\_connections times work\_mem should stay under 1,533 MiB, since one query can use work\_mem several times over. PostgreSQL's documentation suggests a quarter of RAM for shared\_buffers on a server of its own.

